<p>Hotel Palacio de Santa Paula occupies a building with two distinct layers of history beneath its Autograph Collection branding. The site was originally home to a twelfth-century Moorish house, predating the Christian conquest of Granada by several centuries, and later became the location of the Convent of Santa Paula, a religious community established in the sixteenth century. Both periods have left their mark on the structure, giving the hotel an unusually deep architectural history even by the standards of a city as old as Granada.</p>
