    contentEn: `<p>A private transfer from Federico García Lorca Granada-Jaén Airport to NH Collection Granada Victoria covers about 17 kilometres and takes around 20 minutes under normal traffic. The airport sits out on the Vega de Granada plain, and the drive into the city follows the A-92 motorway before joining the Ronda Sur and heading toward Puerta Real, the square at the very centre of Granada where the hotel is located at number 3. Your driver tracks your flight in real time, waits at arrivals with a name board, and takes you directly to the hotel rather than leaving you to work out directions into the heart of the old town on your own.</p>
<p>Puerta Real sits right at the edge of Granada's historic centre, and the streets leading into it from the surrounding avenues carry a good deal of traffic, particularly during the working day. Because the square also functions as a hub for the city's bus network, the final approach benefits from a driver who knows how to time the drop-off and where a vehicle can pull in without adding to the congestion around the square itself. You can check live arrival information at <a href="https://www.aena.es">aena.es</a> before you fly, and arrange the whole journey — pickup point, flight number, and price — in advance through <a href="/get-a-quote/">get a quote</a>.</p>
<p>The same private service runs in reverse for your departure, with a driver collecting you from the hotel at the time you specify and taking you straight back to the terminal. Given how central this address is, having both legs of the journey arranged in advance removes any uncertainty about where a taxi could realistically stop near a busy square, letting you focus on your stay rather than the logistics of arrival and departure.</p>
<h2>About NH Collection Granada Victoria</h2>
<p>NH Collection Granada Victoria sits on Puerta Real 3, right on the square that has long marked the meeting point between Granada's historic centre and its newer southern districts. From the hotel, it's about a three-minute walk to the Cathedral and the adjoining Royal Chapel, putting two of the city's most significant Christian-era monuments within a couple of minutes of the front door.</p>
<p>The hotel operates under the NH Collection brand, the upper tier of the NH Hotel Group's portfolio, typically applied to properties in landmark buildings or particularly central locations within a city rather than to every NH property across a destination. A Puerta Real address fits that positioning well, since the square is about as central as an address in Granada can be, sitting directly on the boundary between the pedestrianised old town and the wider avenues of the modern city.</p>
<p>Puerta Real itself takes its name from a former gate in Granada's city walls, long since gone, though the square retains its role as a key crossing point for the city. Reyes Católicos, one of Granada's principal shopping streets, runs from the square toward the Cathedral and the old Alcaicería silk market, while Gran Vía de Colón extends north from the same junction. Being positioned exactly at this crossroads means the hotel sits within walking reach of several different parts of the city rather than being oriented toward just one neighbourhood.</p>
<p>Beyond the Cathedral and Royal Chapel, the Alhambra is roughly a twenty-minute walk from the hotel, a route that climbs steadily from the city centre up toward the hill where the fortress and palace complex stands above the Darro valley. That distance is manageable on foot for guests who enjoy walking, particularly since much of the route passes through the Realejo quarter and the wooded approach path, though many guests prefer a taxi for the climb, especially in the heat of summer or when visiting first thing in the morning for an early entry slot.</p>
<h3>Who This Hotel Suits</h3>
<p>Travellers who want a genuinely central address within walking distance of the Cathedral, the main shopping streets, and — with a somewhat longer walk — the Alhambra, are the clearest fit for NH Collection Granada Victoria. Its position on a major square also suits business travellers who value straightforward access and proximity to the city's transport hub, along with anyone who prefers a well-known international hotel brand over an independent boutique property.</p>
<h3>Puerta Real as Granada's Crossroads</h3>
<p>Puerta Real functions less like a quiet plaza and more like the working junction of the city, where several of Granada's busiest streets converge and where much of the local bus network passes through. Staying right on this square means being close to the pulse of everyday Granada rather than tucked away in a quieter residential pocket, which suits travellers who want to step straight out into an active, well-connected part of the city rather than needing a walk or a taxi just to reach the main sights.</p>
<h3>Three Minutes to the Cathedral, Twenty to the Alhambra</h3>
<p>The contrast between these two distances says a lot about how to plan a stay here. The Cathedral and Royal Chapel are close enough to visit on a whim, even between other plans, while a visit to the Alhambra is better treated as a dedicated outing, given both the distance and the fact that entry to the monument itself requires a timed ticket. Guests often use the hotel's central position to handle the Cathedral, Royal Chapel, and Alcaicería on foot at leisure, then arrange a taxi or private car specifically for the Alhambra visit to arrive at the correct entrance on time.</p>
<h2>Getting There from the Airport</h2>
<p>The drive from Granada Airport follows the A-92 motorway and the Ronda Sur before entering the city centre near Puerta Real, a route your driver adjusts for traffic and time of day. Traffic around the square itself can be busy throughout the day given its role as a transport hub, so a driver familiar with the current layout and the best drop-off point adds real value on the final approach.</p>
<p>Arranging the transfer in advance means there's no need to negotiate a taxi fare or explain a central address to a driver unfamiliar with the square's layout — your driver already knows exactly where to stop, and a suitable vehicle can be arranged ahead of time for families or groups travelling with extra luggage.</p>
<h2>Planning Your Transfer</h2>
<p>Given the hotel's position at one of the busiest junctions in the city, booking both the arrival and departure legs of your transfer together is the simplest way to handle a stay here. See our <a href="/granada/">Granada</a> page for more on the destination, or <a href="/granada-airport-transfer/">Granada airport transfer</a> for general arrival details, and if your visit includes side trips beyond the city, our <a href="/city-to-city-transfers/">city-to-city transfers</a> service covers onward travel across the region.</p>`,
